{"id":"360416156","kind":"article","title":"死记硬背（填鸭式学习）","author":"Piotr Wozniak","original_authors":["Piotr Wozniak"],"original_source_urls":["https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Cramming"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"学校教育问题","date":"2021-03-27","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":49,"comment_count":2,"minutes":1,"chars":532,"keywords":["死记硬背","间隔重复","长期记忆","学习动机","SuperMemo"],"summary":"词条把死记硬背界定为短间隔内集中复习，指出它或许能应付考试，却可能因连贯性差、干扰和短期记忆而损害长期保持及学习兴趣；并区分考前筛选集复习，称后者可能有益。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/360416156","restoration":null,"toc":[],"html":"<p data-pid=\"zWo46608\"><b>死记硬背</b>是一种在匆忙中集中学习的形式（如考试前的最后一个晚上）。<b>死记硬背</b>会导致记忆的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Coherence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">连贯性</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>差。连贯性低意味着你可以通过考试，但仍然<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Kevin_Kruse:_School_serves_mindless_cramming\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">知之甚少</a>。</p><p data-pid=\"xSqjqC6i\">死记硬背可以帮助你通过考试，但它也是非常有害的。它真的会<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/How_schools_can_contribute_to_Alzheimer's_disease\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">伤害你的大脑</a>或健康。它会影响你<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Pleasure_of_learning\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">对学习的热爱</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>。它产生的短期记忆，会通过<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Interference\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">干扰</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>很快被遗忘。但是，如果对同一学习材料反复使用，<b>死记硬背</b>会导致<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Toxic_memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">毒性记忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup>。只有当你现在需要快速掌握大量知识一段时间，<b>死记硬背</b>才是有用的。你千万不要<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Sleep_and_learning\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">在晚上死记硬背</a>。</p><p data-pid=\"6uyJV12e\">在 <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/SuperMemo\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SuperMemo</a> 的语境中，<b>死记硬背</b>是指任何间隔时间短于<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Optimum_interval\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">最佳间隔</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup>的集中复习。事实证明，死记硬背实际上会<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Spacing_effect\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">削弱记忆</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup>，或者通过<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Interference\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">干扰</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>导致加速<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Forgetting\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">遗忘</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup>。</p><p data-pid=\"tHjFozAv\">相反，以恢复分解的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Coherence\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">知识结构</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>为目的的<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Subset_review\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">筛选集复习</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup>可能是有益的。考试前的筛选集复习可能是不可避免的。考前<b>死记硬背</b>可以帮助你通过考试，但也会削弱长期记忆。</p><p data-pid=\"qrLLg7Sc\">另请参考：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"dTQdKVUg\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/50_bad_habits_learned_at_school\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">学校让学生沾染上的 100 条恶习</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-10\"><a href=\"#ref-10\">[10]</a></sup></li><li data-pid=\"JdDUffFW\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Semantic_learning\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">语义学习</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-11\"><a href=\"#ref-11\">[11]</a></sup>（与死记硬背相反）</li><li data-pid=\"gG1ysIXE\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Serendipitous_impact_of_mindless_cramming\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">死记硬背是如何帮助发展渐进阅读的？</a></li><li data-pid=\"R4s0E2VR\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://twitter.com/guillemlearner/status/1316811830669512706/photo/1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">幽默</a></li></ul><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"sc86LKcE\">原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://supermemo.guru/wiki/Cramming\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Cramming - supermemo.guru</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 一致性与连贯性(Consistency vs Coherence) <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"264327134\" href=\"#/post/264327134\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 学习的乐趣 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"1578551193\" href=\"#/post/1578551193\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 学习的乐趣 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"602150910\" href=\"#/post/602150910\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 干扰 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"269974053\" href=\"#/post/269974053\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 毒性记忆 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"67390960\" href=\"#/post/67390960\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-6\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-6\">↩</a> 最优间隔 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"584041631\" href=\"#/post/584041631\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-7\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-7\">↩</a> 间隔效应 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"279166945\" href=\"#/post/279166945\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-8\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-8\">↩</a> 遗忘 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"558542113\" href=\"#/post/558542113\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-9\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-9\">↩</a> 筛选组学习 <a href=\"https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/subset_learning\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.yuque.com/supermemo/wiki/subset_learning</a></li><li id=\"ref-10\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-10\">↩</a> 学校让人沾染上的 100+ 恶习 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"559705516\" href=\"#/post/559705516\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-11\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-11\">↩</a> 语义学习 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"266922623\" href=\"#/post/266922623\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"359603059","title":"自律的危害","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":273,"minutes":12,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 学校教育问题"},{"id":"360820529","title":"直接教学法","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":9,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 学校教育问题"},{"id":"67390960","title":"9 毒性记忆","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":227,"minutes":24,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"264327134","title":"一致性与连贯性","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":60,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"602150910","title":"学习的乐趣","author":"Piotr Wozniak","votes":1152,"minutes":88,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[],"rec_answers":[{"id":"2202895186","title":"为什么我的成绩那么好，最终还是成了一个没用的人？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":3390,"minutes":35,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 3390 赞同","evidence":"回答中的原生引用/链接以“死记硬背（填鸭式学习）”明确指向目标译文标题或可唯一指向的关键词。"},{"id":"89082348961","title":"十多年的应试教育扼杀了我的好奇心和求知欲，我该怎么办？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes":2470,"minutes":20,"reason":"核心节选引用 · 2470 赞同","evidence":"逐对核验：回答中的直接脚注链接以目标标题或对应概念词指向该译文。"},{"id":"2334764105","title":"我们的教育是究竟为了培养(育)人还是淘汰人？","author":"Thoughts Memo","votes